# Example ReRDMFT input file: water molecule, SCF stopped after 2
# iterations on purpose -- the density is far from converged, so the
# analytic/numerical orbital gradients printed under DEBUG TRUE are
# large instead of the near-zero values seen at a converged stationary
# point (see water_debug.inp for the converged case). NON_REL's
# finite-difference check tests the (HOMO-1, LUMO) pair specifically
# (not HOMO/LUMO) since HOMO/LUMO are symmetry-decoupled in water's C2v
# point group and would read ~0 regardless of convergence. VERBOSE 1
# additionally runs the GeneralizedFock.h dense-2-RDM (O(n^5)) cross-
# check, both in the gradient-norm summary and element-wise in the
# finite-difference report.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
DEBUG TRUE
VERBOSE 1
MAX_ITERATIONS 2

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
